      "versionNonce": 803197002,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775949533696,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Consistency vs Availability for a Comment Feed ⚖️\n\n\nWhat Consistency Would Mean Here\n\n→ Every viewer sees every comment, in the same order, at the same time\n→ A slightly lagging replica could cause some viewers to momentarily miss a comment\n\nWhy Consistency Doesn't Matter Here ✅\n\n→ Comments are ephemeral and contextual — missing one for 500ms is imperceptible at\nvolume\n→ The comment appears shortly after anyway\n→ Nobody is making decisions based on precise ordering of \"lol\" vs \"let's go!!\" 😄\n\nWhat Unavailability Would Mean ❌\n\n→ Comment feed stops entirely — no posting, no viewing\n→ On a live stream this is immediately obvious — users notice and complain within\nseconds\n\nThe Underlying Principle\n\n→ Comment feeds are additive and low-stakes — stale data causes no real harm\n→ Compare to high-stakes systems:\n→ 🏦 Bank transfer — stale data → double spending\n→ 🎟️ Ticket booking — stale data → overselling\n→ 💬 Comment feed — stale data → viewer sees comment 200ms later → nothing\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "drsrvDXe_9StgowHKlSNW",
      "originalText": "Consistency vs Availability for a Comment Feed ⚖️\n\n\nWhat Consistency Would Mean Here\n\n→ Every viewer sees every comment, in the same order, at the same time\n→ A slightly lagging replica could cause some viewers to momentarily miss a comment\n\nWhy Consistency Doesn't Matter Here ✅\n\n→ Comments are ephemeral and contextual — missing one for 500ms is imperceptible at volume\n→ The comment appears shortly after anyway\n→ Nobody is making decisions based on precise ordering of \"lol\" vs \"let's go!!\" 😄\n\nWhat Unavailability Would Mean ❌\n\n→ Comment feed stops entirely — no posting, no viewing\n→ On a live stream this is immediately obvious — users notice and complain within seconds\n\nThe Underlying Principle\n\n→ Comment feeds are additive and low-stakes — stale data causes no real harm\n→ Compare to high-stakes systems:\n→ 🏦 Bank transfer — stale data → double spending\n→ 🎟️ Ticket booking — stale data → overselling\n→ 💬 Comment feed — stale data → viewer sees comment 200ms later → nothing\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
