      "seed": 177501270,
      "version": 661,
      "versionNonce": 1955692874,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1775949163003,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Hysteresis — Two Thresholds Instead of One ⚖️\n\n\nThe Problem it Solves\n\n→ Noisy viewership signal fluctuating around a single threshold (e.g. 100 viewers) causes\nconstant mode switching\n→ Each SSE connection open/close is not free — drains connection pool, triggers\nreconnect logic, emits log noise\n→ At scale, this flapping is genuinely expensive 💸\n\n\nSingle Threshold (Bad)\n\n→ Count ticks above 100 → switch to SSE\n→ Count dips below 100 → tear it down\n→ Noisy signal = constant thrashing back and forth\n\n\nTwo Thresholds with Buffer Zone (Good) ✅\n\n→ Switch up to SSE only when viewership rises decisively above upper threshold\n→ Switch down to polling only when viewership falls well below lower threshold\n→ Fluctuations within the buffer zone → no mode switch triggered\n→ Gap absorbs the noise\n\n\nTuning the Gap\n\n→ Too narrow → still flap\n→ Too wide → SSE runs longer than needed, holding connections open when polling\nwould be cheaper\n→ Common starting point: ±20–30% around your target threshold\n\n\nTradeoff:\nHysteresis adds logic complexity and a tuning parameter that needs ongoing calibration\n— but that cost is almost always worth it over the operational expense of flapping at\nscale ⚖️",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "Q8klulN5R9S42Zy3rCfLT",
      "originalText": "Hysteresis — Two Thresholds Instead of One ⚖️\n\n\nThe Problem it Solves\n\n→ Noisy viewership signal fluctuating around a single threshold (e.g. 100 viewers) causes constant mode switching\n→ Each SSE connection open/close is not free — drains connection pool, triggers reconnect logic, emits log noise\n→ At scale, this flapping is genuinely expensive 💸\n\n\nSingle Threshold (Bad)\n\n→ Count ticks above 100 → switch to SSE\n→ Count dips below 100 → tear it down\n→ Noisy signal = constant thrashing back and forth\n\n\nTwo Thresholds with Buffer Zone (Good) ✅\n\n→ Switch up to SSE only when viewership rises decisively above upper threshold\n→ Switch down to polling only when viewership falls well below lower threshold\n→ Fluctuations within the buffer zone → no mode switch triggered\n→ Gap absorbs the noise\n\n\nTuning the Gap\n\n→ Too narrow → still flap\n→ Too wide → SSE runs longer than needed, holding connections open when polling would be cheaper\n→ Common starting point: ±20–30% around your target threshold\n\n\nTradeoff:\nHysteresis adds logic complexity and a tuning parameter that needs ongoing calibration — but that cost is almost always worth it over the operational expense of flapping at scale ⚖️",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
