      "updated": 1775951821940,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Single-Table Design — Two Access Patterns, Two Key Structures\n\nBase Table\n→ commentId + createdAt = guaranteed unique address per comment\n→ Optimised for direct single-comment lookups\n\n\nGSI — byVideo\n\nGSI: byVideo\n- PK: videoId  (or videoId#shard)\n- SK: createdAt\n\n→ DynamoDB automatically projects base table writes into the GSI\n→ Physically co-locates all comments for the same video, sorted by createdAt\n→ Enables efficient per-video chronological queries without touching base table structure\n\n\nQuery Pattern\n\n{\n    \"TableName\": \"comments\",\n    \"KeyConditionExpression\": \"liveVideoId = :liveVideoId AND commentId < :cursor\",\n    \"ExpressionAttributeValues\": {\n        \":liveVideoId\": \"liveVideoId\",\n        \":cursor\": \"last_comment_id\"\n    },\n    \"ScanIndexForward\": false,\n    \"Limit\": \"pageSize\"\n}\n\nKeyConditionExpression: videoId = :v AND commentId < :cursor\nScanIndexForward: false\nLimit: 10\n\n\nSharding on the GSI 🔥\n→ Plain videoId as GSI PK concentrates a viral video's writes onto one GSI partition\n→ Fix: store videoId#0, videoId#1 etc. — spreads writes across N GSI partitions\n\n\nTradeoff:\nSharded GSI solves hot partition write pressure, but reads must now fan out across all N\nshards in parallel and merge-sort by createdAt before returning a page — read\ncomplexity is the price of write scalability ⚖️",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "mPg7IJt3pvVmHmCzRCWhO",
      "originalText": "Single-Table Design — Two Access Patterns, Two Key Structures\n\nBase Table\n→ commentId + createdAt = guaranteed unique address per comment\n→ Optimised for direct single-comment lookups\n\n\nGSI — byVideo\n\nGSI: byVideo\n- PK: videoId  (or videoId#shard)\n- SK: createdAt\n\n→ DynamoDB automatically projects base table writes into the GSI\n→ Physically co-locates all comments for the same video, sorted by createdAt\n→ Enables efficient per-video chronological queries without touching base table structure\n\n\nQuery Pattern\n\n{\n    \"TableName\": \"comments\",\n    \"KeyConditionExpression\": \"liveVideoId = :liveVideoId AND commentId < :cursor\",\n    \"ExpressionAttributeValues\": {\n        \":liveVideoId\": \"liveVideoId\",\n        \":cursor\": \"last_comment_id\"\n    },\n    \"ScanIndexForward\": false,\n    \"Limit\": \"pageSize\"\n}\n\nKeyConditionExpression: videoId = :v AND commentId < :cursor\nScanIndexForward: false\nLimit: 10\n\n\nSharding on the GSI 🔥\n→ Plain videoId as GSI PK concentrates a viral video's writes onto one GSI partition\n→ Fix: store videoId#0, videoId#1 etc. — spreads writes across N GSI partitions\n\n\nTradeoff:\nSharded GSI solves hot partition write pressure, but reads must now fan out across all N shards in parallel and merge-sort by createdAt before returning a page — read complexity is the price of write scalability ⚖️",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
